<html>
<head>
	<title></title>
</head>
<body style="height: auto; min-height: auto;">Ref No: {{{Case.Case_Number__c}}}<br />
<br />
Hi {{{Case.First_Name__c}}},&nbsp;<br />
<br />
Thank you for contacting the Qantas Customer Care team about your booking from {{{Case.Departure_City__c}}} to {{{Case.Arrival_City__c}}}.<br />
<br />
<em><strong>If unhappy with Change Fees use:</strong></em><br />
<br />
I’m sorry to hear that you’re unhappy with the cost of changing your ticket. To make sure that we meet all our customers’ needs, we offer a variety of fare types.<br />
<br />
I’ve looked into your booking and can see that the fare you purchased via our website was one of our sale fares, and fees apply when making changes. &nbsp;For more information, please head to our <a href="https://www.qantas.com/au/en/book-a-trip/flights/schedule-of-fees.html#change-booking-fees">Change Bookings Fees</a>&nbsp;page.<br />
<br />
<em><strong>If booked online add:</strong></em><br />
<br />
<strong>Our fare conditions</strong><br />
<br />
I understand that you might be disappointed about this outcome. &nbsp;Our Fare Conditions are displayed on the main booking page of qantas.com and customers are asked to accept the conditions by checking the box stating ‘I have read and accept the Fare Conditions above’ before they can complete their booking.<br />
<br />
Providing this information means our customers can choose the fare that’s best for their needs.<br />
<br />
<strong><em>If booked via Contact Centres add:</em></strong><br />
<br />
<strong>Our fare conditions</strong><br />
<br />
I understand that you might be disappointed about this outcome. Our Fare Conditions are explained at the time of booking, &lt;and I can see that our staff advised you of this when you called to book on X&gt;. &nbsp;Providing this information means our customers can choose the fare that’s best for their needs.<br />
<br />
<em><strong>If unhappy with assisted Booking Fee:</strong></em><br />
<br />
<strong>Assisted Booking Fee</strong><br />
<br />
I understand that you might be disappointed with being charged on an assisted booking fee. We charge a fee when you make a booking through our Contact Centres or Airport Sales Desks to cover the administration costs, you do not have to pay this fee when booking online via our website.<br />
<br />
<strong><em>If unhappy with assisted Change Fee:</em></strong><br />
<br />
<strong>Assisted change fee</strong><br />
<br />
I understand that you might be disappointed with being charged an assisted change fee. We introduced the option for our customers to avoid service fees by being able to make simple changes themselves online via our website.<br />
<br />
Making changes that call for the specialised service and expertise of our Contact Centre, Airport, or Social Media teams does attract a fee, which helps contribute to the administration costs of processing your reservation.<br />
<br />
Because of the type of change requested, I'm unable to offer you a refund on this occasion.<br />
<br />
Although we can’t offer a refund, your travel insurance policy might cover these sorts of situations. Let me know if you’d like me to provide you with an insurance letter to assist with a claim.</body>
</html>